            <ArticleTitle>Balanced analgesia after hysterectomy: the effect on outcomes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>176-80, 199</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Balanced analgesia (an opioid and a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory agent) after hysterectomy often leads to better postoperative pain outcomes. Researchers compared post-hysterectomy patients who received balanced analgesia with those who received only morphine patient-controlled analgesia, and their relationship with pain scores, ambulation, and hospital length of stay.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
